concept.human_rationale:
```text
================================================================================
FIREFOX UI MEMORY OPTIMIZATION: ZERO-FOOTPRINT ABLATION PIPELINE
================================================================================

// --- PART 1: THE ENGINE OVERHEAD (THE "HIDDEN MATH") ---
// The Gecko engine treats hidden/0-byte UI nodes as first-class citizens.
// CSS `display: none` or 1x1 transparent SVGs DO NOT stop rendering calculations.
// The engine still executes the following for the lifecycle of the tab:
//
// 1. DOM Allocation: C++ object instantiation in RAM for the node.
// 2. Layout & Reflow: Bounding box, margin, padding, and flex computation.
// 3. Network/Cache Polling: JS controllers request/decode favicon data.
// 4. Accessibility Tree: Node mapping to OS-level accessibility APIs.
// 5. CSSOM Parsing: Memory retention of CSS rules for the hidden element.
//
// SOLUTION: Source-level ablation. Elements must be physically ripped from 
// the source tree BEFORE compilation so the binary linker never sees them.


// --- PART 2: AUTOMATED PIPELINE IMPLEMENTATION ---
// Execution Matrix (Run prior to `./mach build`):
// 1. Markup Ablation -> 2. CSS Purge -> 3. JS Neuter -> 4. Manifest Unlink


// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: MARKUP ABLATION (XHTML / HTML / XUL)
// Objective: Prevent DOM node instantiation via regex stream editing.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

#!/bin/bash
TARGET_CLASSES="tab-icon-image|tab-icon-overlay|bookmark-icon"

# Scorch the UI directories for standard image tags and custom element nodes
find browser/ toolkit/ -type f \( -name "*.xhtml" -o -name "*.html" -o -name "*.inc" \) -exec sed -i -E \
  "/<(image|img|svg)[^>]*class=\"[^\"]*($TARGET_CLASSES)[^\"]*\"[^>]*>/d" {} +


// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: CASCADING STYLE SHEETS (CSS) PURGING
// Objective: Eliminate CSS Object Model (CSSOM) memory overhead.
// Method: State-machine brace depth tracking (Regex fails on nested CSS).
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# python_css_purge.py
import sys, re

def purge_css_block(filepath, target_classes):
    with open(filepath, 'r') as f:
        content = f.read()

    for cls in target_classes:
        # Match class name and find the opening brace
        pattern = re.compile(r'([^{]*\.' + cls + r'[^{]*)\{')
        while match := pattern.search(content):
            start_idx = match.start()
            depth = 1
            curr_idx = match.end()

            # Track brace depth to ensure complete block deletion
            while depth > 0 and curr_idx < len(content):
                if content[curr_idx] == '{': depth += 1
                elif content[curr_idx] == '}': depth -= 1
                curr_idx += 1

            # Slice out the entire CSS block
            content = content[:start_idx] + content[curr_idx:]

    with open(filepath, 'w') as f:
        f.write(content)

purge_css_block('browser/themes/shared/tabs.inc.css', ['tab-icon-image', 'tab-icon-overlay'])


// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: LOGIC NEUTERING (JAVASCRIPT / C++ / RUST)
// Objective: Dead Code Elimination (DCE) to prevent background polling & leaks.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# JAVASCRIPT: Neuter the UI controllers by forcing an immediate return.
# This prevents TypeError loop crashes when the markup is missing.
sed -i '/_updateIcon(aURI)/,/^  }/c\  _updateIcon(aURI) { return; }' \
  browser/base/content/tabbrowser-tab.js

// ---

// RUST (Core Engine Context): 
// If modifying servo/webrender logic, use macro isolation to drop binary weight.
#[cfg(not(feature = "disable_ui_icons"))]
fn allocate_icon_buffer(size: usize) -> Buffer {
    Buffer::new(size)
}

#[cfg(feature = "disable_ui_icons")]
fn allocate_icon_buffer(_size: usize) -> Buffer {
    Buffer::empty() // Compiler executes zero-cost abstraction
}


// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: ASSET MANIFEST UNLINKING (SVG / PNG / ICO)
// Objective: Prevent the packaging script (`mach package`) from compiling 
// assets into `omni.ja` or the executable, saving disk I/O and package weight.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

#!/bin/bash
TARGET_ASSETS="default.png|icon16.svg|bookmark.svg"

# Strip specific asset lines from packaging instructions (jar.mn files)
find browser/ toolkit/ -name "jar.mn" -exec sed -i -E \
  "/($TARGET_ASSETS)/d" {} +

================================================================================

```
